# Sauron Security Directives

- Zero hardcoded credentials, API keys, passwords, or tokens in source files or configuration.
- Prohibit dynamic string evaluation (`eval`, `exec`, `Invoke-Expression`).
- Parameterize all database queries. Raw string concatenation in SQL or ORMs is strictly prohibited.
- Enforce runtime validation schemas (Zod or Pydantic) on all boundary data ingestion points.
